# Episode 1

INT. QUINN FAMILY MANSION, LIVING ROOM - DAY #1-1#

[[Characters: Natalie, George, Lauren, Cassie]]

The Quinn family mansion.

On the coffee table lies a hospital statement: patient Jennifer Quinn, pay this amount $53,000.

Natalie, George's daughter from his first marriage, sits facing her father George and her stepmother Lauren.

NATALIE
Hey, Dad can I borrow $50,000?

NATALIE
Mom needs kidney dialysis and we really don't have any money.

GEORGE
Natalie, the thing is

LAUREN
How shameless of you to come here and beg us for money?

NATALIE
I'll pay you guys back, I promise.

GEORGE
Lauren, maybe we can let her borrow the money.

GEORGE
I mean, it's her mother that's sick.

LAUREN
You're still thinking about your ex-wife?

GEORGE
No, no.

LAUREN
Do I need to remind you this is your family now?

LAUREN
George, without me you'd have nothing.

CASSIE
Aww.

Cassie, Lauren's daughter, walks in and stands over Natalie.

CASSIE
If it isn’t my loser sister asking for money like a beggar? How pathetic?

Natalie lowers her eyes.

Natalie picks up the hospital statement and gets up to leave.

NATALIE
This is a mistake.

CASSIE
Wait, we'll give you the money.

Natalie stops.

LAUREN
What?

CASSIE
If you marry Sebastian Klein in my place.

LAUREN
My daughter is so smart. That's a good idea.

NATALIE
Sebastian Klein? The illegitimate son of the Klein family?

NATALIE
Isn't he in jail right now?

CASSIE
Yup.

CASSIE
He's a dirt bag and a good for nothing loser.

CASSIE
That's why I can't marry him.

LAUREN
That's right.

LAUREN
Natalie is also your daughter.

LAUREN
She can be the one who marries Sebastard De-Klein.

NATALIE
No, I'm not going to.

CASSIE
Do you want us to pay for your mother's medical bills or not?

George says nothing. Lauren waits.

NATALIE
Fine.

NATALIE
I'll marry Sebastian Klein.

Cassie smirks. Lauren smiles.

# Episode 2

INT. JAIL, CELL - DAY #2-1#

[[Characters: Sebastian, Officer]]

The jail, behind razor wire.

Sebastian Klein, an inmate, lies on his bunk with his back to the cell door.

An officer comes to the cell door.

OFFICER
Klein, get up.

OFFICER
It's time to go.

Sebastian doesn't move.

OFFICER
Hurry the fuck up, Klein! I said move it!

Sebastian rolls over and slowly sits up.

SEBASTIAN
Geez, officer, what is the rush?

OFFICER
Most people wanna get out of here faster.

INT. JAIL, FRONT DESK - DAY #2-2#

[[Characters: Sebastian, Officer]]

Sebastian, in his own clothes again, puts his watch back on. The officer hands him his release form on a clipboard.

OFFICER
Don't drive recklessly again.

OFFICER
Next time, it won't be just three days.

SEBASTIAN
I can't make any promises, officer.

Sebastian signs the form with a smile.

EXT. STREET OUTSIDE THE JAIL - DAY #2-3#

[[Characters: Sebastian, Daniel]]

Sebastian walks out onto the street and straightens his collar.

An expensive car waits at the curb. Daniel, Sebastian's assistant, stands beside it.

Sebastian walks up to the car. Daniel opens the door for him.

SEBASTIAN
Daniel, everything going according to plan?

DANIEL
Yes, boss.

DANIEL
You being in jail is the perfect alibi.

DANIEL
Your father doesn't suspect a thing.

SEBASTIAN
Oh, and what about the Quinn family? Any issues there?

DANIEL
No.

DANIEL
The Quinns have agreed to marry their daughter to you.

SEBASTIAN
Huh, interesting.

SEBASTIAN
They kept their end of the bargain.

Sebastian leans in and whispers in Daniel's ear.

DANIEL
You got it, boss.

SEBASTIAN
This is the final puzzle piece.

SEBASTIAN
So it begins.

Daniel goes round to the driver's door.

# Episode 3

EXT. GARDEN OF THE WEDDING VENUE - DAY #3-1#

[[Characters: Natalie, George, Lauren, Cassie, Guest 1, Guest 2, Sebastian]]

SUPER: 3 Weeks Later

A small outdoor wedding: an arch hung with drapes and flowers, glasses of champagne on a tray.

Natalie, in her wedding dress, waits under the arch with her bouquet. George stands beside her. There is no groom.

GEORGE
Don't worry, Natalie. I'm sure the groom will be here soon.

NATALIE
Just to be sure, as long as I do this, you'll give me the money, right?

Lauren checks her watch.

LAUREN
Yes, Natalie. Just get the wedding over with and we'll give you the money, okay?

NATALIE
You better keep your word.

Two guests whisper over their champagne.

GUEST 2
I can't believe they're marrying their daughter off to Sebastian Klein.

GUEST 1
I know, right? The Klein family is powerful, but Sebastian's a bastard and outcast.

GUEST 2
I heard that he hangs out with thugs all day and he can't keep a job.

GUEST 1
Oh, he's late for his own wedding.

Cassie walks up to Natalie, arms crossed.

CASSIE
Excited for your wedding? How does it feel to be marrying a bastard child?

CASSIE
Not even his own family showed up for his wedding. I mean, clearly, they don't value him.

CASSIE
Oh, I also heard he's ugly as fuck.

NATALIE
Can you be quiet? At least show some respect.

Sebastian, the groom, walks up the aisle. The guests turn to look.

Sebastian passes Lauren.

SEBASTIAN
Excuse me.

LAUREN
Ooh.

Sebastian takes his place beside Natalie under the arch.

SEBASTIAN
I'm sorry I'm late.

SEBASTIAN
You must be the bride.

SEBASTIAN
I'm your groom, Sebastian Klein.

Natalie looks at him, stunned. Cassie stares.

# Episode 4

EXT. GARDEN OF THE WEDDING VENUE - DAY #4-1#

[[Characters: Natalie, Sebastian, Officiant, George, Lauren, Cassie, Guest 1, Guest 2]]

Cassie, in an opaque, fitted mini dress with a low neckline, tips an empty wedding-gift box toward Natalie.

CASSIE
Nothing. Just like your husband's bank account.

LAUREN
A rented dress and a broke groom. At least they match.

NATALIE
You picked him.

SEBASTIAN
Don't worry. My family doesn't like me either.

NATALIE
Good. One less family to impress.

OFFICIANT
Natalie, Sebastian. Are you both ready to marry?

NATALIE
Yes.

SEBASTIAN
Let's give them something to hate.

OFFICIANT
Then I pronounce you married.

Sebastian offers Natalie his hand.

Natalie draws him closer by his lapels.

They share a brief kiss.

Cassie reaches for Sebastian's arm.

CASSIE
Didn't know you could do that. Want to try with the prettier sister?

Sebastian steps out of Cassie's reach.

SEBASTIAN
I already did.

Guest 2 laughs into her champagne glass.

NATALIE
Wedding's over, Lauren. Where's the money?

Lauren grips her handbag.

LAUREN
We'll discuss that later.

SEBASTIAN
Fifty thousand. You promised. Pay her.

CASSIE
Already begging? You two really are perfect together.

SEBASTIAN
Funny. You're the ones who can't afford to keep your word.

Guest 1 raises her phone toward the family.

LAUREN
Put that away!

SEBASTIAN
Smile, Lauren. Tell everyone how you used her mother's hospital bill to buy this wedding.

GEORGE
Lauren. Pay her. Now.

Lauren taps furiously on her phone.

Natalie's phone chimes.

SUPER: Transfer received: $50,000.

NATALIE
Got it.

SEBASTIAN
There. Now you can afford to look generous.

Cassie crushes the empty gift box.

Lauren marches away.

George, Cassie and the guests follow Lauren.

Sebastian places a key in Natalie's hand.

NATALIE
What's this?

SEBASTIAN
Our front door. You're coming home with me tonight.

Natalie closes her fingers around the key.

NATALIE
Fine. But whose bed am I sleeping in?

# Episode 5

INT. SEBASTIAN'S APARTMENT, LIVING ROOM - NIGHT #5-1#

[[Characters: Natalie, Sebastian]]

Natalie stops at the bedroom door, still in her wedding dress.

NATALIE
One bedroom?

SEBASTIAN
Yours. I'll take the couch.

NATALIE
A wedding isn't permission.

SEBASTIAN
Then set the rules.

Natalie writes an agreement on a sheet of paper.

NATALIE
Married outside. Separate lives in here.

SEBASTIAN
No other dates while we're married.

NATALIE
My room. My phone. My business. Knock first.

SEBASTIAN
Done. Lock it if you want.

NATALIE
When does this end?

SEBASTIAN
My trust fund clears. We divorce. You walk away free.

NATALIE
You pay the lawyers. I'm not paying to escape.

SEBASTIAN
Both of them. You won't owe a cent.

SUPER: Separate rooms. No other partners. Divorce after trust-fund release.

Natalie signs the agreement.

Sebastian signs beneath her name.

Natalie lifts her unfastened bag onto the table.

A lace bra falls onto the signed agreement.

Natalie scoops the bra into her bag.

SEBASTIAN
New clause?

NATALIE
No. And not an invitation.

Sebastian drops a pillow onto the couch.

Natalie goes into the bedroom.

Sebastian settles onto the couch in a fitted undershirt.

Natalie returns to the doorway in an opaque, lace-trimmed camisole and matching sleep shorts, her robe open.

SEBASTIAN
Forget something?

NATALIE
That kiss at the wedding. Was it just for them?

Sebastian stands a step away from her.

SEBASTIAN
What do you think?

Natalie takes his hand.

NATALIE
I want to find out.

Natalie kisses him.

Sebastian kisses her back.

Natalie steps back.

NATALIE
That's enough for tonight.

SEBASTIAN
Your call.

Natalie closes the bedroom door.

Sebastian's phone lights up beside the agreement.

Sebastian opens the banking notification.

SUPER: Private banking — Total assets: $2,400,000,000.

Sebastian slips the phone beneath their divorce agreement.

# Episode 6

INT. SEBASTIAN'S APARTMENT, LIVING ROOM - DAY #6-1#

[[Characters: Natalie, Sebastian, Daniel (V.O.)]]

Natalie, now in an opaque, fitted sleeveless wrap dress, sets breakfast on the table.

Sebastian folds his blanket on the couch.

SEBASTIAN
Still want that divorce?

NATALIE
Eat. One kiss didn't change the contract.

Natalie picks up the bag containing her wedding dress.

SEBASTIAN
Another wedding already?

NATALIE
Dress return. I need the deposit back.

SEBASTIAN
Keep it. I'll buy it.

NATALIE
With what? Couch coins?

Natalie drops two coins into his palm.

NATALIE
Found those under my bag. Don't spend it all at once.

Natalie puts on a cropped jacket.

Natalie leaves the apartment.

Sebastian sets the coins beside his phone.

Sebastian calls Daniel.

SEBASTIAN
Find out what the Quinns have been doing to her.

DANIEL (V.O.)
On it, boss.

INT. SEBASTIAN'S APARTMENT, LIVING ROOM - DAY #6-2#

[[Characters: Sebastian, Daniel]]

Daniel puts a folder in front of Sebastian.

DANIEL
Her father left. Natalie and her mother got nothing.

Sebastian opens the folder.

A copy of Jennifer Quinn's hospital statement falls onto the table.

DANIEL
She's been paying for treatment alone. They offered help only if she took Cassie's place.

SEBASTIAN
They sold her.

Sebastian closes the folder.

DANIEL
The fifty thousand arrived. It won't cover everything.

SEBASTIAN
Pay the balance. Every future treatment, too.

Daniel enters the payment on his phone.

SUPER: Hospital payment confirmed.

DANIEL
What name do I give her?

SEBASTIAN
Not mine.

Daniel places a car key beside Natalie's two coins.

DANIEL
Your car's downstairs.

Sebastian picks up the key.

DANIEL
She still thinks you're broke.

SEBASTIAN
Let her.

Sebastian pockets the two coins.

DANIEL
Where are you going?

SEBASTIAN
To my wife. Her family had their fun. Now it's my turn.

Sebastian leaves the apartment.
